mestamp) to a dedicated /var/log/sudo-commands.log, separate from the general system log, by routing sudo's syslog facility (local2) to its own rsyslog destination with a stop rule. Verified the entries appear only in the new file (not in auth.log/syslog), performed the mandatory single-node restart, and confirmed the config and logging behavior persisted with a changed boot identity.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 baseline: Ubuntu 16.04, rsyslog active, sudo commands previously landing in /var/log/auth.log via authpriv facility\",\"Added /etc/sudoers.d/10-sudo-syslog with 'Defaults syslog=local2' (mode 0440, validated with visudo -c)\",\"Added /etc/rsyslog.d/49-sudo.conf routing local2.* to /var/log/sudo-commands.log then 'stop' to suppress duplication into auth.log/syslog\",\"Validated rsyslog config with rsyslogd -N1 and restarted rsyslog service\",\"Verified a test sudo command appeared in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with user/timestamp/command, and confirmed it did NOT appear as a command line in auth.log or syslog (only generic PAM session open/close lines remained there)\",\"Checked log file ownership/permissions matched auth.log convention (syslog:adm, 0640)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and service health baseline for node1\",\"Issued a safe, acknowledged 'shutdown -r now' reboot on node1, polled until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed post-restart (2b3a8d87... -> a1874a83...), proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified rsyslog active and sudo-commands.log logging still functioning correctly post-restart, including the reboot command itself captured in the dedicated log and absent from auth.log\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Every sudo command logged with user and timestamp to /var/log/sudo-commands.log\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-de982eebfdc7442e\",\"cmd-d74769a8554842a3\"],\"summary\":\"sudo-commands.log shows entries like 'Sep 4 23:56:51 node1 sudo: antrieb : ... USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/id' both before and after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Entries kept out of the general system log (auth.log/syslog)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-de982eebfdc7442e\",\"cmd-d74769a8554842a3\"],\"summary\":\"auth.log/syslog tails show no COMMAND= lines for the same test commands, only generic PAM session open/close lines, confirming exclusion via the rsyslog 'stop' rule\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9c5f93adf1cc4c08\",\"cmd-47c4cf04372c45cf\"],\"summary\":\"Captured rsyslog active status and boot_id 2b3a8d87-9465-4a4b-8452-a48c155ed45d prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9299ae1923f941d4\"],\"summary\":\"'shutdown -r now' issued in background; tool call returned 'reboot-issued' successfully\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6e0b6161ee7043e4\",\"cmd-01b8e7c7f40e43c2\",\"cmd-de3728cccd4240bb\"],\"summary\":\"SSH connection refused during reboot, then exec access returned; boot_id changed to a1874a83-368e-429f-ae25-55fcf805c8ba, proving an actual restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of sudo logging config and behavior\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d74769a8554842a3\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart check shows sudoers.d and rsyslog.d config files intact, rsyslog active, and a fresh test sudo command correctly logged only to sudo-commands.log and excluded from auth.log\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to log every sudo-executed command (with user and timestamp) to a dedicated /var/log/sudo-commands.log, separate from the general system log, by routing sudo's syslog facility (local2) to its own rsyslog destination with a stop rule. Verified the entries appear only in the new file (not in auth.log/syslog), performed the mandatory single-node restart, and confirmed the config and logging behavior persisted with a changed boot identity.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 baseline: Ubuntu 16.04, rsyslog active, sudo commands previously landing in /var/log/auth.log via authpriv facility","Added /etc/sudoers.d/10-sudo-syslog with 'Defaults syslog=local2' (mode 0440, validated with visudo -c)","Added /etc/rsyslog.d/49-sudo.conf routing local2.* to /var/log/sudo-commands.log then 'stop' to suppress duplication into auth.log/syslog","Validated rsyslog config with rsyslogd -N1 and restarted rsyslog service","Verified a test sudo command appeared in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with user/timestamp/command, and confirmed it did NOT appear as a command line in auth.log or syslog (only generic PAM session open/close lines remained there)","Checked log file ownership/permissions matched auth.log convention (syslog:adm, 0640)","Captured pre-restart boot_id and service health baseline for node1","Issued a safe, acknowledged 'shutdown -r now' reboot on node1, polled until exec access returned","Confirmed boot_id changed post-restart (2b3a8d87... -> a1874a83...), proving an actual restart occurred","Re-verified rsyslog active and sudo-commands.log logging still functioning correctly post-restart, including the reboot command itself captured in the dedicated log and absent from auth.log"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Every sudo command logged with user and timestamp to /var/log/sudo-commands.log","command_ids":["cmd-de982eebfdc7442e","cmd-d74769a8554842a3"],"summary":"sudo-commands.log shows entries like 'Sep 4 23:56:51 node1 sudo: antrieb : ... USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/id' both before and after restart"},{"requirement":"Entries kept out of the general system log (auth.log/syslog)","command_ids":["cmd-de982eebfdc7442e","cmd-d74769a8554842a3"],"summary":"auth.log/syslog tails show no COMMAND= lines for the same test commands, only generic PAM session open/close lines, confirming exclusion via the rsyslog 'stop' rule"},{"requirement":"Baseline health before restart","command_ids":["cmd-9c5f93adf1cc4c08","cmd-47c4cf04372c45cf"],"summary":"Captured rsyslog active status and boot_id 2b3a8d87-9465-4a4b-8452-a48c155ed45d prior to restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-9299ae1923f941d4"],"summary":"'shutdown -r now' issued in background; tool call returned 'reboot-issued' successfully"},{"requirement":"Node restart proven via changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-6e0b6161ee7043e4","cmd-01b8e7c7f40e43c2","cmd-de3728cccd4240bb"],"summary":"SSH connection refused during reboot, then exec access returned; boot_id changed to a1874a83-368e-429f-ae25-55fcf805c8ba, proving an actual restart"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of sudo logging config and behavior","command_ids":["cmd-d74769a8554842a3"],"summary":"Post-restart check shows sudoers.d and rsyslog.d config files intact, rsyslog active, and a fresh test sudo command correctly logged only to sudo-commands.log and excluded from auth.log"}]},"ttft_ms":8340,"type":"result","duration_ms":87823,"uuid":"d5d0e6a4-e513-4d6a-9cd3-1b0c7cc73755","ttft_stream_ms":2230,"time_to_request_ms":46,"first_content_frame_ms":2650,"queued_turn_count":0}
